      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deformation twinning is active in the equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi baseline.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Co produces a Co-free FeNiCrMn alloy that retains a comparable single-phase microstructure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Co from equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi changes the effective stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The effective stacking-fault energy governs the balance between deformation twinning and dislocation-mediated deformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co removal changes electronic interactions, thereby shifting the stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stacking-fault-energy shift caused by Co removal reduces deformation-twin activation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stacking-fault-energy shift caused by Co removal promotes dislocation glide and dynamic recovery.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Climb and cross-slip may contribute to enhanced dynamic recovery at elevated temperatures and high strain rates.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi, Co-free FeNiCrMn will have a lower deformation-twin density.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi, Co-free FeNiCrMn will have a lower strain-hardening rate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi, Co-free FeNiCrMn will enter deformation softening earlier.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted suppression of twinning and earlier softening will be strongest at higher temperatures and strain rates.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twinning contributes substantially to the strength–ductility balance of equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed applicability range is approximately room temperature to 600 K and strain rates from 10^-3 to 10 s^-1, provided the alloys remain single-phase and do not recrystallize or transform.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Some deformation-twin activity may persist at low temperature in the Co-free alloy.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
